  <div class="note">
    <span class="lbl">The most common misunderstanding</span>
    The seismic catalogue <strong>does not produce the rates</strong>. Rates come from the moment balance: the Gutenberg-Richter <em>a</em> parameter is solved by equating the moment the plate accumulates with the moment the earthquakes release. The GCMT events only move the branches' <strong>weights</strong>, from prior to posterior. Turn LEVEL 3 off and you still have complete rates.
  </div>
